          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3. (i) The cost of a notebook is twice the cost of a pen. Consider the cost of a notebook to be ₹t and that of a pen to be "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "{ \\mathfrak { F } } p ."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Charlie wrote "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "t = 2 p ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , whereas Meera wrote "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "p = 2 t ."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Which of these two representations is correct?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.188,
            0.75,
            0.883,
            0.873
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) In a one-day International Cricket match between India and Sri Lanka played in Nagpur, two Indian batsmen together scored 176 runs. Manisha expressed this situation as "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "x + y = 176"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , where the number of runs scored by one batsman is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "X ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and the number of runs scored by the other is y. Is this a correct representation?"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
